        {
          "id": "SP_ALCYONIDIUM_PARASITICUM",
          "name": "Alcyonidium parasiticum",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Alcyonidium",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>Colonies form a thick greyish brown cylindrical encrustation around the stems of hydroids and erect bryozoans. The colour of the colonies is largely due to the build up of fine silt and mud particles on the colony surface. When these particles are brushed away it is possible to see numerous hair like-filaments that are likely to be trapping the sediment particles. The borders of the autozooids are often unclear but the zooids appear to be roughly hexagonal in shape. They measure approximately 0.2 mm in diameter. </p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:4985523"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ALCYONIDIUM_PEDUNCULATUM_ROBERTSON_1902",
