        {
          "id": "SP_ALCYONIDIUM_POLYOUM",
          "name": "Alcyonidium polyoum",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Alcyonidium",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>Colonies of this species are thin and encrusting; they can grow to several centimeters across depending upon the availability of the algal substrate. Autozooids at the growing edge often have an iridescent sheen and become a deep brown as they get older. The autozooids are polygonal in shape measuring 0.5-0.8 x 0.2-0.4mm. </p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:4985522"
        },
